<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the project code. The function `lldpd_alloc_hardware` calls `lldpd_clone_port` with `cfg->g_default_local_port` as the `source` argument. However, `cfg->g_default_local_port` is not initialized in the fuzz driver, and the project code does not check if it is NULL before dereferencing it in `lldpd_clone_port`.

A potential patch would be to add a NULL check in `lldpd_clone_port` before calling `lldpd_port_serialize`.

```c
// in lldpd.c
void
lldpd_clone_port(struct lldpd_port *destination, struct lldpd_port *source)
{
u_int8_t *output = NULL;
ssize_t output_len;
struct lldpd_port *cloned = NULL;

if (source == NULL) {
log_warnx("alloc", "source port is NULL, cannot clone");
return;
}

output_len = lldpd_port_serialize(source, (void **)&output);
if (output_len == -1 ||
lldpd_port_unserialize(output, output_len, &cloned) <= 0) {
log_warnx("alloc", "unable to clone default port");
free(output);
return;
}
// ...
}
```
</crash-analysis>

